 established:-
 (i) The death of a woman should be caused by burns  or bodily injury or otherwise than under a 'normal  circumstance' (ii) such a death should have  occurred within seven years of her marriage;
 (iii) she must have been subjected to cruelty or  harassment by her husband or any relative of her  husband;
 (iv) such cruelty or harassment should be for or in  connection with demand of dowry ; and  (v) such cruelty or harassment is shown to have been  meted out to the woman soon before her death.
